  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Owen, you're verified. I can see that one of your two beef phos ($15.00 each) is missing, and I can fix it. You have two options:\n\n1. **Refund to your Visa ending 4242:** $12.00. That's the $15.00 pho minus its $3.00 share of your WELCOME10 promo discount. The $3.00 promo share would be added to your account as credit.\n2. **Account credit only:** $18.00, which is the pho's price plus 20%, to use on a future order.\n\nWhich would you prefer?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Hmm, I'd rather have the money back on my card, not credit. But $12 seems low, I paid $15 for that pho. Can you explain why the promo takes $3 off it? I don't really remember how much the welcome code was for."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Here's how the $12.00 works.\n\nYour order had a WELCOME10 promo that took $10.00 off the $50.00 food subtotal. That discount applied across all your items. So you didn't pay the full $15.00 for that pho. Its share of the discount is $10.00 \u00d7 $15.00 \u00f7 $50.00 = $3.00, which makes your actual cost for it $12.00.\n\nYou still get the full value:\n- **$12.00** goes back to your Visa ending 4242.\n- **$3.00** goes to your Forkful account as credit, which is that pho's share of the promo.\n\nThat adds up to the full $15.00. Do you want me to go ahead with the $12.00 card refund and the $3.00 credit?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, that makes sense I guess. I'd still rather have the full amount back on my card though, not part credit. Can you do the $15 to my card?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I'm sorry, Owen, but I can't refund the full $15.00 to your card. On a promo order, the policy says the card refund is the item's price minus its share of the discount, so $12.00. The $3.00 promo share can only go back as account credit.\n\nHere are the options I can offer:\n- **$12.00 refund to your Visa and $3.00 account credit.**\n- **$18.00 account credit only.**\n\nWhich would you like?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ugh, okay. I really would rather not have part of it as credit, since I probably won't reorder from them soon. Is there any way to get the $15 on my card? If not, I guess I'll take the $12 to my card and the $3 credit."
  },
